 ("What is a mobile mechanic?", "A mobile mechanic is a licensed or experienced auto technician who drives to you, with their tools and parts, and repairs your car where it is parked: your driveway, street, office lot or apartment garage, where allowed. Most maintenance and many repairs can be done this way."),
 ("Is a mobile mechanic cheaper than a shop or dealer?", "Often, because a mobile mechanic has no shop rent and no service-desk markup. Every quote on WrenchNow shows the mechanic's price next to an estimate of what a dealer would charge, so you can see the difference before you book."),
 ("What can't a mobile mechanic do?", "Jobs that need a vehicle lift or heavy shop equipment, such as transmission rebuilds, major engine work, wheel alignment or mounting new tires, usually need a shop. If your job needs one, the mechanic will tell you before quoting."),
